### 2.1 Centralised error‑handling middleware

Right now the code never calls `next(err)` and there’s no catch‑all error handler. If an exception bubbles up, Express will send a generic HTML stack trace in development and a plain “Error” in production – both are sub‑optimal.

**Add a middleware stack like:**

```js
// After all routes
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const err = new Error('Not Found');
  err.status = 404;
  next(err);
});

app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  // Log the error (use your logger)
  console.error(err);

  // Hide internal details from the client
  const status = err.status || 500;
  const message = status === 500 ? 'Internal Server Error' : err.message;

  res.status(status).json({
    error: {
      message,
      // Optionally expose a request‑id for tracing
      // requestId: req.id
    },
  });
