## 4️⃣ Additional Hardening Tips (quick checklist)

| Checklist Item | Implementation |
|----------------|----------------|
| **Disable `x-powered-by` header** | `app.disable('x-powered-by');` |
| **Force HTTPS** (if behind a proxy) | `app.enable('trust proxy');` <br>`app.use((req, res, next) => { if (req.secure) return next(); res.redirect('https://' + req.headers.host + req.url); });` |
| **Content Security Policy** (via Helmet) | `helmet.contentSecurityPolicy({ directives: { defaultSrc: ["'self'"] } })` |
| **Avoid path traversal** when serving static files | Use `express.static` with a safe root and never concatenate user input into file paths. |
| **Graceful shutdown** (catch `SIGTERM`, `unhandledRejection`) | ```js<br>process.on('unhandledRejection', err => { console.error(err); process.exit(1); });<br>process.on('SIGTERM', () => { server.close(() => process.exit(0)); });``` |
| **Dependency health** | Run `npm audit` regularly, consider `npm i -g npm-check-updates` and keep libraries up‑to‑date. |
| **Secrets management** | Store API keys, DB passwords, etc., in environment variables or a secret manager; never hard‑code them. |

---

## 5️⃣ Putting It All Together – Refactored `app.js`

Below is a **ready‑to‑paste** version that incorporates all of the above (minus the optional `POST /users` example, which you can add later).  

```js
// app.js – hardened Express server (security‑first)

require('express-async-errors');          // must be first
const express = require('express');
